From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xilin Wu <sophon@radxa.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 10:06:55 +0000
Subject: media: i2c: rk628: Port vendor driver to Linux 7.0 and CAMSS

Integrate the RK628 driver into the media I2C build and update timer and
HDMI codec callbacks for the current kernel interfaces. Remove Rockchip
CIF and HDMI RX class dependencies, expose attributes on the I2C device,
and use optional NVMEM storage for HDCP keys.

Adapt the CSI subdevice for Qualcomm CAMSS with a bridge entity and
UYVY8_1X16 bus format. Keep link frequency, pixel rate, frame intervals
and formats consistent with the detected HDMI timings. Allow optional
module metadata and reference clocks for self-clocked bridge modules.

Fix probe cleanup and work/IRQ handling across suspend and removal.
Process receiver interrupt status when polling without an IRQ. On
RK628F/H modules without a cable-detect GPIO, keep HPD and the receiver
active while waiting for a TMDS clock instead of repeatedly reporting
PHY lock failures. Return ENOLINK when no input signal is detected.

Signed-off-by: Xilin Wu <sophon@radxa.com>
